1. e4 { All the lines are based on extensive and careful analysis as well as grandmaster and correspondence play. We consulted all the major sources (books, DVDs etc.) and found a lot of improvements (in some cases even refutations) . Here is the list of the sources where we checked what other authors recommend for White. Books: Martyn Kravtsiv - “The Italian Renaissance” (Quality Chess 2020) Larry Kaufman - “Kaufman's New Repertoire for Black and White” (New In Chess 2019) Milos Pavlovic - “The Modernized Scotch Game” (Thinkers Publishing 2019) Alexander Khalifman and Sergei Soloviov - “Squeezing 1.e4 e5: a Solid Strategic Approach” (chess-stars 2019) Alexander Delchev - “Bc4 against the Open Games” (New In Chess 2018) Christof Sielecki - “Keep it Simple 1.e4” (chessable/New In Chess 2018) John Shaw - “Playing 1.e4. Caro-Kann, 1...e5 and Minor Lines” (Quality Chess 2016) Karsten Muller & Georgios Souleidis - 'Winning with the Slow (but Venomous!) Italian' (New In Chess 2016) Yelena Dembo & Richard Palliser - “The Scotch Game” (Everymanchess 2011) John Emms - “Beating 1e4 e5” (Everyman 2010) Vladimir Barsky - “The Scotch Game for White” (Chess Stars 2009) D.Taylor & K.Hayward - 'Play the Ponziani' (Everymanchess 2009) Jan Piński - “Italian Game and Evans Gambit” (Everymanchess 2005) Alexander Khalifman - “Opening for White According to Anand vol. 1” (Chess Stars 2003) Joshua Doknjas - 'Opening Repertoire: The Ruy Lopez' (Everymanchess 2019) Videos/DVDs/Online: Fabiano Caruana - “Navigating the Ruy Lopez” (Chessbase DVD) Parimarjan Negi - “The Modern Scotch Opening” (Chessbase DVD) Ivan Saric - “A new look at the Italian (Giuoco Piano) ” (chess24) Sergei Tiviakov - “The Bishop’s Opening and The Italian Game” (ChessBase DVD) Nigel Davies - “Attack with The Modern Italian” (ChessBase DVD) Simon Williams - “Rocket Repertoire: The Four Knights” (ChessBase DVD) Simon Williams - “Evans Gambit for the new generation” (ChessBase DVD) Christof Sielecki - "Keep It Simple: 1. e4" (chessable) Nils Grandelius - “The Grand Ruy Lopez” (chessable) S.P. Sethuraman - “Lifetime Repertoires: Sethuraman's 1. e4 - Part 1” (chessable) Wesley So - “Lifetime Repertoires: Wesley So's 1. e4 - Part 1” (chessable) } 
